1. **An image-stabilization system comprising:**

a first deformable optical membrane and a second deformable optical membrane disposed in an optical path;

a fluid chamber shared by the first and second deformable optical membranes, the fluid chamber containing an optically transmissive fluid such that deformation of either deformable optical membrane changes an optical characteristic of the system;

a first actuation device operatively coupled to the first deformable optical membrane;

a second actuation device operatively coupled to the second deformable optical membrane; and

a controller configured to receive a signal indicative of image motion and, based on the signal, selectively energize either the first actuation device or the second actuation device to deform the respective deformable optical membrane and thereby compensate for the image motion.
